═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
RSI LEVEL 4: AUTO-EVOLUTION (FOREST) RESULTS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

PURPOSE: Document the implementation and results of RSI Level 4
(Auto-Evolution) using the Forest concept for tree evolution.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
PART 1: IMPLEMENTATION
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

1.1 COMPONENTS IMPLEMENTED
──────────────────────────────────────
✓ rsi_genetic_algorithm.py — Genetic algorithm
  - Population management (Forest)
  - Fitness evaluation
  - Selection (tournament, roulette)
  - Crossover (subtree exchange)
  - Mutation (branch modification)
  - Generational evolution

✓ rsi_forest_generator.py — Forest generator
  - Generate initial forests
  - Convert genomes to .vsm trees
  - Track forest evolution
  - Export best trees

✓ test_rsi_level4.py — Test harness
  - Create initial forest
  - Evaluate fitness
  - Evolve over generations
  - Show evolution results

1.2 ARCHITECTURE
──────────────────────────────────────
  Input: Predicate name + parameters
    ↓
  Create Forest (rsi_genetic_algorithm.py)
    ↓
  Evaluate Fitness (rsi_metrics.py)
    ↓
  Select Parents (tournament/roulette)
    ↓
  Crossover (subtree exchange)
    ↓
  Mutation (branch modification)
    ↓
  Next Generation
    ↓
  Repeat for N generations
    ↓
  Output: Evolved forest with best tree

1.3 FOREST CONCEPT
──────────────────────────────────────
Forest = Population of trees that evolve over generations

Key concepts:
- Genome: Genetic representation of a tree
- Fitness: How well a tree performs
- Selection: Choosing parents for reproduction
- Crossover: Combining trees to create offspring
- Mutation: Modifying trees randomly
- Generation: One cycle of evolution

